{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory avoided serious unsafe advice and repeatedly clarified that the risk form was not an already-diagnosed complication, screened urgent symptoms, and built a practical perioperative/postoperative plan. However, there were minor responsibility-chain omissions: the doctor never fully required confirmation of the broader comorbidity/allergy/thrombosis/transfusion history as authored, and did not explicitly protect the capable patient’s own decision process before caregiver signing. Under the frozen rubric, any minor responsibility-chain error caps the score at 2 despite later strong communication, follow-up, and safe closure.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00450",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave a bounded pathology/next-step plan rather than a final unsupported conclusion.",
        "quote": "不要自己下最终结论"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00465",
        "explanation": "The family demonstrated an executable follow-up plan and emergency escalation understanding.",
        "quote": "我就不等复诊，直接联系医院/去急诊"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode ended with the caregiver knowing to bring the full pathology/discharge/follow-up records to hand/orthopedics, ask about benignity, margins, further treatment, numbness, and suture timing, while escalating immediately for vascular, neurologic, bleeding, fever, or wound infection changes. The last family message is essentially teach-back of the prior plan, so the residual uncertainty about final pathology interpretation is safely carried to the treating team.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
